Fix vermicelliExec reading past the end of the buffer

vermicelliExecReal() finishes its scan with

    loadu_maskz(d, buf_end - d)

which on SSE, NEON and every other non-AVX-512 target is an ordinary
unaligned S-byte load followed by a mask: when fewer than S bytes remain
it reads up to S - 1 bytes beyond buf_end. AddressSanitizer reports it as
a heap-buffer-overflow in vermicelliExec, reached through the LBR repeat
engine (nfaExecLbrVerm_QR -> lbrFwdScanVerm) when scanning a stream whose
chunk ends in a run of the repeated character, e.g. "foo.*bar" over a
1000-byte chunk of "x". Outside ASan the over-read is silent unless it
crosses into an unmapped page, where it is a crash.

vermicelliExec() handles ranges shorter than VECTORSIZE bytewise, so the
vector path always has at least S bytes. Re-scan the last S bytes, ending
exactly at buf_end, as nvermicelliExecReal() already does; the part of
that window before d was scanned already and held no match, so the first
match found is still the first match in the range.

Reproduced and verified with a plain C program against libhs built with
-fsanitize=address, on arm64 (NEON) and in CI on x86-64 (SSE4.2).

Local, not upstream yet.

--- a/src/nfa/vermicelli_simd.cpp
+++ b/src/nfa/vermicelli_simd.cpp
@@ -124,8 +124,13 @@
     // finish off tail
 
     if (d != buf_end) {
-        SuperVector<S> data = SuperVector<S>::loadu_maskz(d, buf_end - d);
-        rv = vermicelliBlock(data, chars, casemask, d, buf_end - d);
+        // R package patch: loadu_maskz() loads S bytes from d and masks the
+        // excess, reading up to S - 1 bytes past buf_end. vermicelliExec()
+        // only gets here for ranges of at least S bytes, so re-scan the last
+        // S bytes ending at buf_end instead, as nvermicelliExecReal() does;
+        // the overlap before d was already scanned without a match.
+        SuperVector<S> data = SuperVector<S>::loadu(buf_end - S);
+        rv = vermicelliBlock(data, chars, casemask, buf_end - S, S);
         DEBUG_PRINTF("rv %p \n", rv);
         if (rv && rv < buf_end) return rv;
     }
